# W30b, b (k10). The lobby's return mat (stagML11 mate02) takes a player to the stage of his last Security Gate
# (dng205b2 point 2, 19.30.1 fact 4): its departure is posted by the depart action (the return mat needs the gate, which
# only dng205b2's GENE-03 wave powers). While a's Dry Land instance has never been at dng205b2, b's arrival there is a NEW
# of its own (I1a; I1b shows a's row greyed "Story not here yet"); home again by its gate disc, and after a reached
# dng205b2 the next arrival there joins a without leaving a's story.
campaign until stage=stagml11,control
idle until epoch>=@250
depart dng205b2 2 until stage=dng205b2,control
log b alone on dng205b2
idle until frames>=300 fail present>=2
disk 8 until stage=stagml11,control
log b home again
idle until epoch>=@520
depart dng205b2 2 until stage=dng205b2,control
wander 0 0 30 until present=2,sealed>=600 fail epoch>=@900
log b joined a on dng205b2
